# idtosdf

- Label: ID to SDF
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 1
- Parameters: 3 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/idtosdf.html
- Summary (EN): Computes a signed distance field from the boundaries where ID values change. Each ID gets its own distance field, so wiring a Tile Pattern id output in creates per-tile SDFs.
- Résumé (FR) : Calcule un champ de distance signé à partir des frontières entre identifiants, avec un champ distinct par identifiant.

- Inputs meaning: ["id: the ID layer whose value changes define the distance"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Invert", "meaning": "flips the sign of the distance; ID fields have no inside or outside, so defaults are positive"}, {"name": "Iterations", "meaning": "how many times the distance is recomputed; 1 is enough for a uniform speed field"}, {"name": "Tile Size", "meaning": "block size used to split work between serial and parallel parts; should not change the converged result"}]

- Caveats: ["The output sdf is a raw distance field; pass it through a downstream node such as SDF to Mono to get a usable image."]

